quiet.md #24: hollow RenderImages and RenderImage::with_scale_factor

RenderImage::hollow makes a copy with the same id and size but no pixels, for
an image already uploaded to the windows' atlases; paint_image skips a hollow
image a window's atlas does not have, records it and asks for another frame,
and Window::take_missing_images hands those ids to the owner, which decodes
them again. with_scale_factor lets a downscaled decode keep the original's
layout size. Document images are decoded at their display size and drop their
pixels once uploaded (docs/MEMORY.md).

